%% alt: Clients call an API gateway, which checks identity and rate limits and routes each path to its service: users or orders. The orders service calls the payments service synchronously to charge, and publishes an order-placed event to an event log, which an email service consumes. Each service owns its own database.
%% caption: Each service owns its data and is reached only through its API. Calls that need an answer go over RPC; the rest flows as events.
flowchart TB
  classDef control fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#1f1147
  classDef data fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#3b2405

  client(["Web and mobile clients"])
  gw{{"API gateway<br/>identity · rate limits · routing"}}:::control
  users["Users service"]
  orders["Orders service"]
  pay["Payments service"]
  email["Email service"]
  udb[("Users DB")]:::data
  odb[("Orders DB")]:::data
  pdb[("Payments DB")]:::data
  log[["Event log"]]

  client --> gw
  gw -- "/users" --> users
  gw -- "/orders" --> orders
  orders -- "RPC: charge" --> pay
  users --> udb
  orders --> odb
  pay --> pdb
  orders -- "order placed" --> log
  log --> email
